# Trivy vulnignore source — single source of truth for image-scan
# (slice-M7 §2.4, ADR 0012 §2.8/§2.9).
#
# The companion file `.security/.trivyignore` is gitignored and
# regenerated by `scripts/render-trivyignore.sh` whenever
# `make image-scan` runs.
#
# Format (one entry per line):
#
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # expires:YYYY-MM-DD  reason: short rationale
#   GHSA-xxxx-xxxx  # expires:YYYY-MM-DD  reason: short rationale
#
# Maintenance contract:
#
#   - `expires:YYYY-MM-DD` is MANDATORY on every entry. Missing or
#     unparseable dates break the renderer.
#   - Entries with `expires` in the past break the renderer; renew
#     or remove. The break is intentional (ADR 0012 §2.8 abs 3).
#   - Default expires horizon: 90 days from the entry-creation
#     commit. Longer horizons need a documented reason.
#   - `reason:` is optional but strongly encouraged — it lands in
#     the rendered `.trivyignore` as an audit comment.
#   - Only the FIRST `expires:` substring on a line is honoured;
#     downstream tools should not rely on multiple `expires:` per row.
#
# (no entries at first release — clean slate.)
